{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgfBy7KU27LvamV9gLyvk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01DLB77eTvvMgbUX6UemJXeX","name":"WebFetch","input":{"url":"https://github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge/tree/main/dist/handoff","prompt":"List the files in this directory and summarize what each is for, including any README instructions on how to use the engine (script tags, APIs, how to build a game, input, audio, animation). Include exact file names and URLs of raw files if available."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7243,"cache_read_input_tokens":17659,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":7243,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"df1bdcb4-3a77-4f4c-afe3-765655b3436d","uuid":"868feeca-19e5-46c7-a1a4-4de8f0240775","timestamp":"2026-11-03T02:16:23.501Z","request_id":"req_011CgfBy6yPUCA2SL87tXKUs","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01DLB77eTvvMgbUX6UemJXeX":{"url":"https://github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge/tree/main/dist/handoff","prompt":"List the files in this directory and summarize what each is for, including any README instructions on how to use the engine (script tags, APIs, how to build a game, input, audio, animation). Include exact file names and URLs of raw files if available."}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgfBy7KU27LvamV9gLyvk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01NuE5wmukvyynYA7hNd9Ptm","name":"WebFetch","input":{"url":"https://github.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/tree/main/lib/hub","prompt":"List the files in this directory and summarize how a game integrates with this multiplayer hub: the protocol, the client API, the required manifest/record fields, the run-record format, and how a game is registered. Include exact file names and any code snippets for the client API."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7243,"cache_read_input_tokens":17659,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":7243,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"df1bdcb4-3a77-4f4c-afe3-765655b3436d","uuid":"b5f967fe-fe4e-4944-be39-ed425e87c5c5","timestamp":"2026-11-03T02:16:24.055Z","request_id":"req_011CgfBy6yPUCA2SL87tXKUs","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01NuE5wmukvyynYA7hNd9Ptm":{"url":"https://github.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/tree/main/lib/hub","prompt":"List the files in this directory and summarize how a game integrates with this multiplayer hub: the protocol, the client API, the required manifest/record fields, the run-record format, and how a game is registered. Include exact file names and any code snippets for the client API."}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NuE5wmukvyynYA7hNd9Ptm","type":"tool_result","content":"**Files in `lib/hub/`**\n\nThe listing shows these files, but it ends with \"View all files,\" so there may be more:\n\n- `examples/` (directory)\n- `README.md`: the protocol specification\n- `bridge.js`\n- `harness.html`: the test harness\n- `retrofit.md`\n- `round.js`\n- `session.js`: the client, pasted unmodified into the game\n\n**Protocol**\n\nThe protocol is \"AI Hub Session Protocol v1.\" A session is up to four players, each on their own device, playing rounds one after another. The hub handles the invite, lobby, seats, network, clock, scoreboard, and results. A game declares one of three modes:\n\n- `parallel`: each copy plays its own round and sends nothing to the others.\n- `ghost`: each copy also shows the other players' characters, which don't affect its own round.\n- `shared-world`: the host's copy runs one world, and the other copies send it their players' actions.\n\n**Manifest fields (HTML meta tags)**\n\nThe page doesn't describe a separate manifest file. Integration is done with tags in the game's `<head>`:\n\n- `hub:session` (value `1`)\n- `hub:session-players` (`MIN-MAX`)\n- `hub:session-mode` (`parallel`, `ghost`, or `shared-world`)\n- `hub:session-goal` and `hub:session-howto`: shown on the hub's card\n- Optional: `hub:session-minutes` and `hub:webgpu` (`required`)\n\n**Client API**\n\nPaste `session.js` as the first script in `<head>`. A minimal sketch based on the documented calls:\n\n```js\nconst info = await AIHub.connect({ mode: 'parallel', seats: [1, 4] });\nif (info === null) { /* no hub: run the game normally */ }\n\nAIHub.ready();                       // call once, when the round can start\nAIHub.on('start', () => { /* play begins when AIHub.time() reaches 0 */ });\nAIHub.on('time-up', ({ graceMs }) => { /* report within graceMs */ });\nAIHub.on('end', ({ reason, standings }) => { /* stop input and sound */ });\n\nAIHub.progress({ score, label });    // parallel and ghost, periodically\nAIHub.result({ time: AIHub.time() });// parallel and ghost, once; lower time wins\nAIHub.finish({ standings, won });    // shared world, host only, once\nAIHub.send(data, { to, reliable });  // ghost and shared world\nAIHub.on('message', (data, from) => { /* ... */ });\nAIHub.rng(label);                    // same numbers on every copy\n```\n\nOther documented members are `AIHub.active`, `AIHub.time()`, `AIHub.fail(message)`, and `AIHub.seeded`. The `info` object includes `me`, `players`, `host`, `isHost`, `server`, `mode`, `round`, `limitMs`, and `seed`.\n\n**Run-record format**\n\nThe page doesn't describe a run-record file format. It does define the result payloads: `result()` takes `time` or `score`, plus optional `stats` and `awards`. `finish()` takes `standings`, plus optional `scores`, `won`, `stats`, and `awards`.\n\n**Registration**\n\nThe page doesn't describe a registration process. It says only that \"The hub tests every game when it joins the library\" and that a game failing the test is kept out of sessions. To test a game locally, serve `harness.html` next to it and open `harness.html?game=GAME.html&players=2&auto=1`. The page also mentions `node scripts/hub-check.mjs <game>` in the AI Hub repository."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"df1bdcb4-3a77-4f4c-afe3-765655b3436d","uuid":"45f7165d-c099-4679-98a4-c4f58d077798","timestamp":"2026-11-03T02:16:34.781Z","tool_use_result":{"bytes":288006,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"**Files in `lib/hub/`**\n\nThe listing shows these files, but it ends with \"View all files,\" so there may be more:\n\n- `examples/` (directory)\n- `README.md`: the protocol specification\n- `bridge.js`\n- `harness.html`: the test harness\n- `retrofit.md`\n- `round.js`\n- `session.js`: the client, pasted unmodified into the game\n\n**Protocol**\n\nThe protocol is \"AI Hub Session Protocol v1.\" A session is up to four players, each on their own device, playing rounds one after another. The hub handles the invite, lobby, seats, network, clock, scoreboard, and results. A game declares one of three modes:\n\n- `parallel`: each copy plays its own round and sends nothing to the others.\n- `ghost`: each copy also shows the other players' characters, which don't affect its own round.\n- `shared-world`: the host's copy runs one world, and the other copies send it their players' actions.\n\n**Manifest fields (HTML meta tags)**\n\nThe page doesn't describe a separate manifest file. Integration is done with tags in the game's `<head>`:\n\n- `hub:session` (value `1`)\n- `hub:session-players` (`MIN-MAX`)\n- `hub:session-mode` (`parallel`, `ghost`, or `shared-world`)\n- `hub:session-goal` and `hub:session-howto`: shown on the hub's card\n- Optional: `hub:session-minutes` and `hub:webgpu` (`required`)\n\n**Client API**\n\nPaste `session.js` as the first script in `<head>`. A minimal sketch based on the documented calls:\n\n```js\nconst info = await AIHub.connect({ mode: 'parallel', seats: [1, 4] });\nif (info === null) { /* no hub: run the game normally */ }\n\nAIHub.ready();                       // call once, when the round can start\nAIHub.on('start', () => { /* play begins when AIHub.time() reaches 0 */ });\nAIHub.on('time-up', ({ graceMs }) => { /* report within graceMs */ });\nAIHub.on('end', ({ reason, standings }) => { /* stop input and sound */ });\n\nAIHub.progress({ score, label });    // parallel and ghost, periodically\nAIHub.result({ time: AIHub.time() });// parallel and ghost, once; lower time wins\nAIHub.finish({ standings, won });    // shared world, host only, once\nAIHub.send(data, { to, reliable });  // ghost and shared world\nAIHub.on('message', (data, from) => { /* ... */ });\nAIHub.rng(label);                    // same numbers on every copy\n```\n\nOther documented members are `AIHub.active`, `AIHub.time()`, `AIHub.fail(message)`, and `AIHub.seeded`. The `info` object includes `me`, `players`, `host`, `isHost`, `server`, `mode`, `round`, `limitMs`, and `seed`.\n\n**Run-record format**\n\nThe page doesn't describe a run-record file format. It does define the result payloads: `result()` takes `time` or `score`, plus optional `stats` and `awards`. `finish()` takes `standings`, plus optional `scores`, `won`, `stats`, and `awards`.\n\n**Registration**\n\nThe page doesn't describe a registration process. It says only that \"The hub tests every game when it joins the library\" and that a game failing the test is kept out of sessions. To test a game locally, serve `harness.html` next to it and open `harness.html?game=GAME.html&players=2&auto=1`. The page also mentions `node scripts/hub-check.mjs <game>` in the AI Hub repository.","durationMs":10722,"url":"https://github.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/tree/main/lib/hub"},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01NuE5wmukvyynYA7hNd9Ptm","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DLB77eTvvMgbUX6UemJXeX","type":"tool_result","content":"## Files and folders in `dist/handoff/`\n\nThe page lists these files. Raw URLs are derived from the GitHub blob links by swapping the host to `raw.githubusercontent.com`. I haven't verified that they resolve.\n\n| File | Purpose | Raw URL |\n|---|---|---|\n| `README.md` | Overview, reading order, and run/test commands | https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge/main/dist/handoff/README.md |\n| `API.md` | The API card: a complete starter game, coordinate meanings, rules, common mistakes, and the API by area | https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge/main/dist/handoff/API.md |\n| `API-INDEX.md` | One-line entry for every public engine name, with signatures, units, and defaults. Meant for searching, not reading whole | https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge/main/dist/handoff/API-INDEX.md |\n| `AI_GUIDE.md` | Recipes by genre, visual targets, frame order, heights, and recorded sessions | https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge/main/dist/handoff/AI_GUIDE.md |\n| `my-3d2dge.js` | The full engine in one readable file, with no dependencies | https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge/main/dist/handoff/my-3d2dge.js |\n| `my-3d2dge-agent.js` | A smaller \"agent edition\" with the essential engine. Games written for it also run on the full engine | https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge/main/dist/handoff/my-3d2dge-agent.js |\n| `index.html` | Listed at the root of the handoff folder; the page doesn't describe its role | https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge/main/dist/handoff/index.html |\n| `package.json` | Pins Playwright for the tools | https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge/main/dist/handoff/package.json |\n\n**Folders** (the page shows only the top level, with \"View all files\" indicating more):\n\n- `docs/`: includes `ASSETS.md`, the card for still objects and materials (`r.shape`, `map.solid`, `E.MATERIALS`).\n- `game/`: the template game (`index.html`, `game.js`, `test.mjs`). Copy it to start a new game.\n- `kits/`: 2D genre kits. Each has a readable `<id>.js` game, a playable `<id>.html`, and a headless `test.mjs`. `kits/README.md` is the table of kits.\n- `modules/`: optional engine modules, each documented in its own header. Load them after the agent edition.\n- `tools/`: `check.mjs` (browser play and error check), `filmstrip.mjs` (frame recording), `replay.mjs` (session replay), and `asset-find.mjs`, `asset-sheet.mjs`, `asset-set.mjs` (asset search, preview, and set creation, with `asset-lib.mjs` as a helper).\n- `src/assets/`: the asset store, with sets converted from CC0 libraries.\n\n## How to use the engine (per the README)\n\n- **Starting point:** Read `API.md` first. Then start from a kit in `kits/` or from `game/`, rather than an empty file.\n- **Running:** Run `npm install` and `npx playwright install chromium` once. Open `game/index.html` in a browser, or serve the folder with `npx serve`.\n- **Testing:** Run `node game/test.mjs` for a headless test, or `node kits/test.mjs <id>` for a kit.\n- **Browser checks:** Run `node tools/check.mjs game/index.html`.\n- **Single-file handoff:** Inline the two scripts into the page.\n- **Construction:** `new E.Game()` runs headless in Node. Menus are configured with `new E.Game({ menu: { items, settings, controls, quit } })`, and heavy setup goes in `game.start({ boot: { steps } })`.\n- **Assets:** Load a set with its script, then call `E.addAssets(window.ASSETS['kenney-furniture'])`.\n- **Input:** `game.input.tap('jump')` presses an action for one step. `game.input.hold('right')` holds it, and `hold('right', false)` releases it.\n- **Time:** `game.advance(seconds)` runs fixed 1/120 s steps, so `advance(1)` runs 120 updates. Results are deterministic.\n- **Debugging:** Set `game.debug = { snapshot(), teleport(x, y, z) }` so tests and tools can read game state.\n\nThe page does not describe the audio API or the animation API in detail. For those, see `API.md`, which the page points to but doesn't excerpt."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"df1bdcb4-3a77-4f4c-afe3-765655b3436d","uuid":"d2b6afde-e123-4907-a03e-6be2951b633e","timestamp":"2026-11-03T02:16:36.474Z","tool_use_result":{"bytes":234260,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"## Files and folders in `dist/handoff/`\n\nThe page lists these files. Raw URLs are derived from the GitHub blob links by swapping the host to `raw.githubusercontent.com`. I haven't verified that they resolve.\n\n| File | Purpose | Raw URL |\n|---|---|---|\n| `README.md` | Overview, reading order, and run/test commands | https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge/main/dist/handoff/README.md |\n| `API.md` | The API card: a complete starter game, coordinate meanings, rules, common mistakes, and the API by area | https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge/main/dist/handoff/API.md |\n| `API-INDEX.md` | One-line entry for every public engine name, with signatures, units, and defaults. Meant for searching, not reading whole | https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge/main/dist/handoff/API-INDEX.md |\n| `AI_GUIDE.md` | Recipes by genre, visual targets, frame order, heights, and recorded sessions | https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge/main/dist/handoff/AI_GUIDE.md |\n| `my-3d2dge.js` | The full engine in one readable file, with no dependencies | https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge/main/dist/handoff/my-3d2dge.js |\n| `my-3d2dge-agent.js` | A smaller \"agent edition\" with the essential engine. Games written for it also run on the full engine | https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge/main/dist/handoff/my-3d2dge-agent.js |\n| `index.html` | Listed at the root of the handoff folder; the page doesn't describe its role | https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge/main/dist/handoff/index.html |\n| `package.json` | Pins Playwright for the tools | https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge/main/dist/handoff/package.json |\n\n**Folders** (the page shows only the top level, with \"View all files\" indicating more):\n\n- `docs/`: includes `ASSETS.md`, the card for still objects and materials (`r.shape`, `map.solid`, `E.MATERIALS`).\n- `game/`: the template game (`index.html`, `game.js`, `test.mjs`). Copy it to start a new game.\n- `kits/`: 2D genre kits. Each has a readable `<id>.js` game, a playable `<id>.html`, and a headless `test.mjs`. `kits/README.md` is the table of kits.\n- `modules/`: optional engine modules, each documented in its own header. Load them after the agent edition.\n- `tools/`: `check.mjs` (browser play and error check), `filmstrip.mjs` (frame recording), `replay.mjs` (session replay), and `asset-find.mjs`, `asset-sheet.mjs`, `asset-set.mjs` (asset search, preview, and set creation, with `asset-lib.mjs` as a helper).\n- `src/assets/`: the asset store, with sets converted from CC0 libraries.\n\n## How to use the engine (per the README)\n\n- **Starting point:** Read `API.md` first. Then start from a kit in `kits/` or from `game/`, rather than an empty file.\n- **Running:** Run `npm install` and `npx playwright install chromium` once. Open `game/index.html` in a browser, or serve the folder with `npx serve`.\n- **Testing:** Run `node game/test.mjs` for a headless test, or `node kits/test.mjs <id>` for a kit.\n- **Browser checks:** Run `node tools/check.mjs game/index.html`.\n- **Single-file handoff:** Inline the two scripts into the page.\n- **Construction:** `new E.Game()` runs headless in Node. Menus are configured with `new E.Game({ menu: { items, settings, controls, quit } })`, and heavy setup goes in `game.start({ boot: { steps } })`.\n- **Assets:** Load a set with its script, then call `E.addAssets(window.ASSETS['kenney-furniture'])`.\n- **Input:** `game.input.tap('jump')` presses an action for one step. `game.input.hold('right')` holds it, and `hold('right', false)` releases it.\n- **Time:** `game.advance(seconds)` runs fixed 1/120 s steps, so `advance(1)` runs 120 updates. Results are deterministic.\n- **Debugging:** Set `game.debug = { snapshot(), teleport(x, y, z) }` so tests and tools can read game state.\n\nThe page does not describe the audio API or the animation API in detail. For those, see `API.md`, which the page points to but doesn't excerpt.","durationMs":12968,"url":"https://github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge/tree/main/dist/handoff"},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01DLB77eTvvMgbUX6UemJXeX","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
