{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0163HqMS3cu443MSNUUijHQu","type":"tool_result","content":"80:- 1000 17d. Perception; E.Suspicion: suspicion\n332:- `input.names = null` †: the actions' names on the Controls screen ({ attack: 'Sword' }; false hides one from rebinding: the game's menu.controls); onBindings(b): called with the player's new bindings (the game saves and applies them)\n427:- `r.prop(name, x, y, z, o = {})` †: set dressing from E.prop: r.prop('torch', x, y, z, { size, color, flip, light: true, halo: true, bias, hides, footprint }) feet on the world point; flames animate and glow. light: true also adds a warm light to game.lights. A prop at least chest high (E.HEIGHTS.chest, 22: a pillar, a statue, a lamp) drawn in front of an x-ray actor shows the actor's silhoue\n431:- `r.sightCone(obs, o = {})` †: an observer's view on the ground: a dithered fan fov wide (radians) about its facing, out to range, cut short where the map hides a body's chest (map.ray, the height rules), draped over the ground below. o: { range: 120, fov: 1.6, facing, map, eye, color: '#ffe080', alpha: .3, rays }. Call it in draw (it is a decal: under walls and bodies)\n471:- `game.allowJoin(o = {})` †: let players join, up to max (2..4): Start on a gamepad no one holds, or 2 on the keyboard (o.keys: false not); onJoin (input, number) as each does. allowJoin(false) closes it (the names split and join are String's and Array's)\n483:- `game.hitFx(x, y, z, o = {})`: everything a good hit needs in one call: hit-stop, shake, an impact star, sparks along the hit direction, a sound, a damage number and a rumble on a gamepad. hitFx(x, y, z, { power: 1, angle, damage, color, sound: 'hit', rumble: true })\n484:- `game.menu(name)`: open the menu (the corner's menu button and the touch START do it): a pausable scene (or a game started without scenes) pauses on its pause screen; any other scene, a title, waits under the settings. menu('settings') or menu('controls') opens that screen. Without a menu (menu: false, or the agent edition) it pauses a scene in play. Returns true when a menu opened\n490:- `game.players` †: the players: [game.input (player 1), ...the ones who joined (game.allowJoin, game.addPlayer: section 10j)]; each an input with player (1..4), name ('P1'), color (E.PLAYER_COLORS) and device. A game of one: [game.input]\n495:- `game.saves()` †: game.saves: the save slots (section 10k), made when first read\n617:- `new E.Saves(game, o) → saves` †: game.saves (made when first read): o is menu.saves ({ slots, version, migrate, write, read })\n636:- `saves.write` †: what a save holds ({ data, place, level })\n640:- `new E.Attack(spec = {}, over) → slash`: new E.Attack(spec) or new E.Attack('slash', { reach: 9 }): a name from E.MOVES plus overrides\n666:- `new E.Humanoid(o = {}) → rig`: new E.Humanoid({ size: 1.3, build, weapon, outfit, hair, hat, sleeves, armor, hood, cape, colors, ... }): a character rig posed from math every step (API.md, \"Characters\", lists the options); update(dt, state) each step, draw(g, ox, oy, view) inside r.actor. hat: 'cap' | 'band' | 'crown' | 'helmet' | 'pointed' (or { style, color }); hood: true (drawn in colors\n703:- `E.MOVES: slash, backslash, overhead, rising, thrust, spin, plunge, twohand, jab, cross, hook, uppercut, haymaker, elbow, ... (24)`: a library of named attacks with timing and body motion (anticipation, lunge, step, twist, hop). new E.Attack('overhead'), new E.Attack('thrust', { reach: 10 }), new E.Combo(['jab', 'cross', 'hook', 'uppercut']) rig.update(dt, { ..., attack: E.move('roundhouse',\n767:- `map.solid(id, x, y, z = 0, o = {})` †: make a shape solid in this map: map.solid(id | entry, x, y, z, o) with r.shape's placement (facing, scale, flip, params) -> the solid ({ x, y (the footprint's middle), z, top, hx, hy, c, s, shape, px, py (where it was placed) }; map.solids holds them; what stands on one sorts after it). A body overlapping its span in height is pushed out of its footpri\n768:- `map.solidAt(x, y)`: solidCell at a world point\n769:- `map.solidCell(cx, cy)`: true where a cell has a wall (or is outside the map); walkable() also counts blocked floor\n773:- `map.wall(from, dir, o = {})` †: the wall face a body touches or faces: from `from`, in direction dir (an angle or [dx, dy]), the first point within reach whose top rises more than a step above its feet. { x, y (on the face), nx, ny (the face's normal, out toward the body), top (how high it rises there), bottom (the floor at its foot), facing (the angle into it) } or null. Cells give axis fa\n817:- `new E.FlowField(map, o = {}) → flow`: new E.FlowField(map, { step: 2, climb: 0, drop: 0, jump: 0 }): distances over the tops a body can stand on (E.HEIGHTS). With no options it covers the floor (and walls no higher than step, which bodies walk over); a target on a roof gets a field across the roofs it connects to\n818:- `new E.FlowField({ step, climb, drop })`: next-door cells connect when their tops differ by at most step, or going up by up to climb and down by up to drop (agents that climb walls or hop down)\n819:- `new E.FlowField({ jump })`: (world units) links tops across a gap that a jump clears, straight along a row or column, by map.landing's rules (up to jumpRise higher, 11, and jumpDrop lower, 18): an agent with E.Mover's leap chases across roofs. With jump, distances are travel: a jump of k cells costs k, and a climb 1 plus its rise in cells (climbing is slow), so a chase leaps a gap rather th\n820:- `flow.dir(x, y, fx, fy)`: normalized ground direction to walk from (x, y) toward the target (straight at it where the field doesn't reach)\n963:- `new E.Mover(o = {}) → mover`: new E.Mover({ x, y, z, r: 5, ... }): any of its fields, below, as options. An E.Body: it has body.jump, push and the body's fields too\n1002:- `new E.Suspicion(o = {}) → suspicion`: new E.Suspicion({ rise, decay, notice, search, alert, forget }): a guard's mind (its fields, below, are its options). Its level rises while it sees the target (faster the more exposed and nearer), decays while it doesn't, and names a state: 'calm', 'notice' (turn and look), 'search' (go to last), 'alert' (chase). An alert guard that loses the target se\n1005:- `suspicion.update(dt, seen, target)` †: one step: seen is E.sees' result (or true / false), target the body seen. Returns the state\n1015:- `E.sees(obs, tgt, o = {})`: can observer see target? { seen, d (ground distance), angle (observer -> target), exposure: 0..1 }. The target must be within range and inside the cone fov wide (radians) about the observer's facing; exposure is the share of three points on it (its feet, its chest, its head) that the observer's eyes see past every top of o.map, times the target's own exposure (de\n1089:- `E.PROPS: torch, candle, candelabra, chandelier, brazier, window, banner, pillar, statue, crate, barrel, chest, pot, sign, fence, lamp, door, tree, pine, bush, flowers, grass, rock, crystal, bones, skull, vines, cobweb, lantern, streetlamp, awning, hydrant, trashcan, firedrum, sandbags, cactus, palm, mushroom` †: the names of the built-in props for r.prop(name, x, y, z, opts) and E.prop(nam\n1097:- `E.shapeBox(id, x, y, z = 0, o = {})`: where a placed shape stands, as both engines collide with it: E.shapeBox(id | entry, x, y, z, { facing, scale, flip, params }) -> { x, y (its footprint's middle), z, top, hx, hy (half its footprint, along its own x and y), c, s (the turn's cosine and sine) }; null for an unknown shape. map.solid makes one solid; world.shape gives it a collider\nShell cwd was reset to /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-haiku-5-5-medium__20261102-191613__xb81546/work","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"df1bdcb4-3a77-4f4c-afe3-765655b3436d","uuid":"974c99e3-0418-4c2d-84f4-ece0be7e0439","timestamp":"2026-11-03T02:17:36.903Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"80:- 1000 17d. Perception; E.Suspicion: suspicion\n332:- `input.names = null` †: the actions' nam