{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012SBTVHsG7fjyTvXnYF4bMM","type":"tool_result","content":"20:- Collision, standing, sight (`map.sight`, `map.ray`), reach (`E.targets`, `E.inArc` with `dz`) and navigation (`E.FlowField`) all follow these rules. `E.dist` is 3D; `E.overlap` is flat.\n166:- `E.inArc(a, facing, b, range, halfAngle, dz)`: melee cone on the ground: is b (with optional radius r) within range of a and within halfAngle of facing? dz (optional) also limits the height difference, so a hero on a roof ca\n196:- `E.px`: the pixel primitives: px.rect, px.line, px.dot, px.disc, px.poly, px.sprite, ... (each snaps to whole pixels)\n200:- `px.disc(g, cx, cy, r, c)`: a filled circle\n204:- `px.line(g, x0, y0, x1, y1, c, w = 1)`: a line w pixels thick, no smoothing\n205:- `px.poly(g, pts, c)`: a filled polygon through [[x, y], ...]\n206:- `px.polyDither(g, pts, c, a, wx = 0, wy = 0)`: translucent polygon: a = 0..1 opacity (stepped alpha, or a dither pattern in 'dither' style). wx/wy = world pixel offset for the pattern\n207:- `px.rect(g, x, y, w, h, c)`: a filled rectangle, snapped to whole pixels\n210:- `E.sprite(rows, colors = {}, scale = 1)`: Pixel sprite written as strings. Each character is one pixel; colors maps a character to a hex color; '.' and ' ' are transparent. scale (whole number) enlarges each pixel. const COI\n361:- `E.font.width(s, o)`: width in pixels of the widest line. opts: a scale number or { font, scale }\nShell cwd was reset to /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-haiku-5-5-medium__20261102-191613__xb81546/work","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"df1bdcb4-3a77-4f4c-afe3-765655b3436d","uuid":"c5d01382-a0d0-479b-877b-b905dbf681fe","timestamp":"2026-11-03T02:21:07.980Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"20:- Collision, standing, sight (`map.sight`, `map.ray`), reach (`E.targets`, `E.inArc` with `dz`) and navigation (`E.FlowField`) all follow these rules. `E.dist` is 3D; `E.overlap` is flat.\n166:- `E.inArc(a, facing, b, range, halfAngle, dz)`: melee cone on the ground: is b (with optional radius r) within range of a and within halfAngle of facing? dz (optional) also limits the height difference, so a hero on a roof ca\n196:- `E.px`: the pixel primitives: px.rect, px.line, px.dot, px.disc, px.poly, px.sprite, ... (each snaps to whole pixels)\n200:- `px.disc(g, cx, cy, r, c)`: a filled circle\n204:- `px.line(g, x0, y0, x1, y1, c, w = 1)`: a line w pixels thick, no smoothing\n205:- `px.poly(g, pts, c)`: a filled polygon through [[x, y], ...]\n206:- `px.polyDither(g, pts, c, a, wx = 0, wy = 0)`: translucent polygon: a = 0..1 opacity (stepped alpha, or a dither pattern in 'dither' style). wx/wy = world pixel offset for the pattern\n207:- `px.rect(g, x, y, w, h, c)`: a filled rectangle, snapped to whole pixels\n210:- `E.sprite(rows, colors = {}, scale = 1)`: Pixel sprite written as strings. Each character is one pixel; colors maps a character to a hex color; '.' and ' ' are transparent. scale (whole number) enlarges each pixel. const COI\n361:- `E.font.width(s, o)`: width in pixels of the widest line. opts: a scale number or { font, scale }","stderr":"\nShell cwd was reset to /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-haiku-5-5-medium__20261102-191613__xb81546/work","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_012SBTVHsG7fjyTvXnYF4bMM","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
