{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgfDtwnrF2coVwACCn1Cq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The phone and ultrawide title layouts both look right. The remaining work is the feedback sections (in-game and in the exit interview), the exit-interview file, and a final full run of every suite on the final build."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3823,"cache_read_input_tokens":272257,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3823,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"df1bdcb4-3a77-4f4c-afe3-765655b3436d","uuid":"abd24198-2cb2-43fe-9565-c27a95436acd","timestamp":"2026-11-03T02:41:43.316Z","request_id":"req_011CgfDtwN4EtsB1Qwe2z4P7"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgfDtwnrF2coVwACCn1Cq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01CMKBD8d8hQqgay3fpVSAsy","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-haiku-5-5-medium__20261102-191613__xb81546/work/HalfBaked-BreakingBad-claude-haiku-5-5-medium-20261102-191613 && python3 -I - <<'EOF'\nimport json, re\ntesting = [\n \"About 14 issues in total, found by my own review, the unit tests and the browser runs. Two were game-breaking: the attract run stalled on its first dialogue (it waited for a key press it never sent), and leaving attract drew one frame with the run state already cleared, throwing an error. The rest were visual or input problems: an apostrophe the font cannot draw, a map with ragged rows, the boss bar covering the HUD, a floor that read as bricks, the V camera key never bound, the attract exit ignoring keys no action uses, and the AI's dash not moving the hero.\",\n \"Two were critical. The attract stall and the attract exit error both broke the attract run, which is a required feature.\",\n \"The full playthrough with real key presses (title, cook, three sales, boss, results): it covers the whole path and found the boss-defeat dialogue was never shown.\",\n \"The viewport matrix: the game draws onto one canvas, so it reports no overflow and no DOM errors almost by construction. It confirmed the layouts, but it could not find game bugs.\"\n]\nengine = [\n \"The scene system, the TileMap with Body and FlowField, Humanoid rigs with E.Combo and E.Attack, and the built-in settings, menu and pause screens. A lot of the game came for free.\",\n \"Yes. Dialog plays one voice per letter with no per-letter variation, so I wrapped audio.sfx to jitter pitch for animalese. game.input.anyPressed() ignores keys that no action uses, so I wrote my own any-input check. The DEFAULT preset puts dash on Space, the same key as confirm, so I wrote a custom binding table. E.Menu's arrow keys counted a disabled item as a stop.\",\n \"The glue: the cook minigame, the sight-and-heat rules, the attract AI, the hub wiring and the animalese hook.\",\n \"Working out the pixel-font limits (no curly quotes or arrows), and the dialogue and attract interplay: a blocking dialogue box stalls any run that has no player.\",\n \"The default input preset. Dash on Space, the same key as confirm, is a problem for keyboard players. I would make presets bind each action explicitly, or warn when two actions share a key.\",\n \"Give the Dialog a per-letter callback, so voices can vary by letter without a wrapper, and let the menu skip disabled items when moving with the arrow keys.\"\n]\nprompt = [\n \"The clear fixed sections: Source Information, Testing, Engine and Prompt Feedback, plus the JSON shape. Without them I would have guessed at the format.\",\n \"How the Usage line should be filled when no cost or token figures are available: I used unknown. Also whether the in-game credits must repeat the feedback sections or only the source information. I did both.\",\n \"Making the game feel complete in one pass: a stealth system, a cook minigame, a boss, attract mode and a hub round, each with its own tests, inside one session.\",\n \"A test with a real pad, run in a browser with a virtual gamepad. I could only fake the pad's state, so the controller paths (stick inversion, PlayStation and Xbox glyphs on a real controller) are checked by reading code, not by playing.\"\n]\nlines_extra = []\nlines_extra.append({\"t\": \"TESTING FEEDBACK\", \"h\": True, \"gap\": 4})\nfor i, a in enumerate(testing, 1): lines_extra.append({\"t\": f\"{i}. {a}\", \"gap\": 2})\nlines_extra.append({\"t\": \"\", \"gap\": 6})\nlines_extra.append({\"t\": \"ENGINE FEEDBACK\", \"h\": True, \"gap\": 4})\nfor i, a in enumerate(engine, 1): lines_extra.append({\"t\": f\"{i}. {a}\", \"gap\": 2})\nlines_extra.append({\"t\": \"\", \"gap\": 6})\nlines_extra.append({\"t\": \"PROMPT FEEDBACK\", \"h\": True, \"gap\": 4})\nfor i, a in enumerate(prompt, 1): lines_extra.append({\"t\": f\"{i}. {a}\", \"gap\": 2})\n# Check ASCII only: the engine font has no curly quotes or dashes.\nfor ln in lines_extra:\n    assert all(ord(c) < 128 for c in ln[\"t\"]), ln[\"t\"]\np = 'src/credits.js'\ns = open(p).read()\nmarker = \"  lines.push({ t: '', gap: 8 });\\n\"\nassert s.count(marker) == 1\ninsert = \"\".join(\"  lines.push(%s);\\n\" % json.dumps(ln) for ln in lines_extra)\ns = s.replace(marker, marker + insert)\nopen(p, 'w').write(s)\nprint('credits lines', len(lines_extra))\nEOF\nnode --check src/credits.js && echo CREDITS_OK","description":"Add testing, engine and prompt feedback to the in-game credits"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3823,"cache_read_input_tokens":272257,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3823,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"df1bdcb4-3a77-4f4c-afe3-765655b3436d","uuid":"4882255c-c01d-42bf-8b11-41f416d781d8","timestamp":"2026-11-03T02:41:51.963Z","request_id":"req_011CgfDtwN4EtsB1Qwe2z4P7","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01CMKBD8d8hQqgay3fpVSAsy":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-haiku-5-5-medium__20261102-191613__xb81546/work/HalfBaked-BreakingBad-claude-haiku-5-5-medium-20261102-191613 && python3 -I - <<'EOF'\nimport json, re\ntesting = [\n \"About 14 issues in total, found by my own review, the unit tests and the browser runs. Two were game-breaking: the attract run stalled on its first dialogue (it waited for a key press it never sent), and leaving attract drew one frame with the run state already cleared, throwing an error. The rest were visual or input problems: an apostrophe the font cannot draw, a map with ragged rows, the boss bar covering the HUD, a floor that read as bricks, the V camera key never bound, the attract exit ignoring keys no action uses, and the AI's dash not moving the hero.\",\n \"Two were critical. The attract stall and the attract exit error both broke the attract run, which is a required feature.\",\n \"The full playthrough with real key presses (title, cook, three sales, boss, results): it covers the whole path and found the boss-defeat dialogue was never shown.\",\n \"The viewport matrix: the game draws onto one canvas, so it reports no overflow and no DOM errors almost by construction. It confirmed the layouts, but it could not find game bugs.\"\n]\nengine = [\n \"The scene system, the TileMap with Body and FlowField, Humanoid rigs with E.Combo and E.Attack, and the built-in settings, menu and pause screens. A lot of the game came for free.\",\n \"Yes. Dialog plays one voice per letter with no per-letter variation, so I wrapped audio.sfx to jitter pitch for animalese. game.input.anyPressed() ignores keys that no action uses, so I wrote my own any-input check. The DEFAULT preset puts dash on Space, the same key as confirm, so I wrote a custom binding table. E.Menu's arrow keys counted a disabled item as a stop.\",\n \"The glue: the cook minigame, the sight-and-heat rules, the attract AI, the hub wiring and the animalese hook.\",\n \"Working out the pixel-font limits (no curly quotes or arrows), and the dialogue and attract interplay: a blocking dialogue box stalls any run that has no player.\",\n \"The default input preset. Dash on Space, the same key as confirm, is a problem for keyboard players. I would make presets bind each action explicitly, or warn when two actions share a key.\",\n \"Give the Dialog a per-letter callback, so voices can vary by letter without a wrapper, and let the menu skip disabled items when moving with the arrow keys.\"\n]\nprompt = [\n \"The clear fixed sections: Source Information, Testing, Engine and Prompt Feedback, plus the JSON shape. Without them I would have guessed at the format.\",\n \"How the Usage line should be filled when no cost or token figures are available: I used unknown. Also whether the in-game credits must repeat the feedback sections or only the source information. I did both.\",\n \"Making the game feel complete in one pass: a stealth system, a cook minigame, a boss, attract mode and a hub round, each with its own tests, inside one session.\",\n \"A test with a real pad, run in a browser with a virtual gamepad. I could only fake the pad's state, so the controller paths (stick inversion, PlayStation and Xbox glyphs on a real controller) are checked by reading code, not by playing.\"\n]\nlines_extra = []\nlines_extra.append({\"t\": \"TESTING FEEDBACK\", \"h\": True, \"gap\": 4})\nfor i, a in enumerate(testing, 1): lines_extra.append({\"t\": f\"{i}. {a}\", \"gap\": 2})\nlines_extra.append({\"t\": \"\", \"gap\": 6})\nlines_extra.append({\"t\": \"ENGINE FEEDBACK\", \"h\": True, \"gap\": 4})\nfor i, a in enumerate(engine, 1): lines_extra.append({\"t\": f\"{i}. {a}\", \"gap\": 2})\nlines_extra.append({\"t\": \"\", \"gap\": 6})\nlines_extra.append({\"t\": \"PROMPT FEEDBACK\", \"h\": True, \"gap\": 4})\nfor i, a in enumerate(prompt, 1): lines_extra.append({\"t\": f\"{i}. {a}\", \"gap\": 2})\n# Check ASCII only: the engine font has no curly quotes or dashes.\nfor ln in lines_extra:\n    assert all(ord(c) < 128 for c in ln[\"t\"]), ln[\"t\"]\np = 'src/credits.js'\ns = open(p).read()\nmarker = \"  lines.push({ t: '', gap: 8 });\\n\"\nassert s.count(marker) == 1\ninsert = \"\".join(\"  lines.push(%s);\\n\" % json.dumps(ln) for ln in lines_extra)\ns = s.replace(marker, marker + insert)\nopen(p, 'w').write(s)\nprint('credits lines', len(lines_extra))\nEOF\nnode --check src/credits.js && echo CREDITS_OK","description":"Add testing, engine and prompt feedback to the in-game credits"}}}
